      "explanation": "'Will have left' describes an action that will be completed before another future time/event \u2014 the marker of the future perfect tense.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Future perfect is like RSVP'ing 'I'll already be gone by the time you arrive' \u2014 the action finishes before the reference point in the future.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f 'Future Indefinite Tense' (simple future) is tempting because of the 'will', but 'have left' (perfect) changes it.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
