      "explanation": "'More...than' (comparative) flips to a negative equal comparison: 'my computer has more functions than yours' means 'yours does NOT have as many as mine'.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 It's like saying 'I have more candy than you' = 'You don't have as much candy as me' \u2014 same fact, stated from the other side.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Option c ('My computer does not have as many...') swaps subject and meaning backwards \u2014 the mirror image of the correct answer.",
