      "explanation": "'Money' is uncountable, so the negative form needs 'much' (not 'many'): 'Not much money has been spent on the project.'\n\n\ud83d\udca1 'Much' pairs with uncountable stuff like money or water; 'many' is for things you can count one by one, like coins.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f 'Not many money' (option a) is a classic countable/uncountable mismatch \u2014 money can't be counted as 'many'.",
