      "options": [
        "Mahatma Gandhi",
        "B.K.Ambedkar",
        "Jawaharlal Nehru",
        "Subhas Chandra Bose"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 2,
      "explanation": "Jawaharlal Nehru is commonly credited with describing communalism as the 'Indian version of fascism', since both mobilise identity-based hatred for political power.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Communalism and fascism are like two different flavoured versions of the same poison \u2014 one uses religion, the other uses race/nation, but both divide people to control them.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Gandhi is tempting since he spoke extensively against communal violence, but this particular framing is attributed to Nehru's political writings.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
      "year": 2016,
      "paperId": "mpsc-inspector-of-taxes-2016-gs-ii"
