      "explanation": "Elite theory was pioneered by Italian sociologists Vilfredo Pareto and Gaetano Mosca, who argued that a small elite always ends up ruling any society.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Think of elite theory as the 'cream always rises to the top' idea \u2014 first bottled and labelled by Italian thinkers Pareto and Mosca.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f American Sociologists is tempting since elite theory is widely taught in US political science today, but its origin is Italian.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
      "year": 2016,
      "paperId": "mpsc-inspector-of-taxes-2016-gs-ii"
