      "topic": "gs1_history",
      "topicLabel": "Gandhian thought",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "Who said \u201cPoverty is the Worst Form of Violence\u201d?",
      "options": [
        "M.N.Roy",
        "M.K.Gandhi",
        "V.K. Saraswa",
        "Dadabhai Naoroji"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 1,
      "explanation": "Mahatma Gandhi said 'Poverty is the worst form of violence', linking economic deprivation to the same harm caused by physical violence.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Gandhi's point is like saying a slow starvation hurts just as much as a punch \u2014 just because poverty doesn't leave a visible bruise doesn't mean it isn't violent.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Dadabhai Naoroji is tempting since he's famous for economic critique (the 'Drain Theory'), but this specific quote is one of Gandhi's most repeated lines.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
