      "subject": "history",
      "topic": "gs1_history",
      "topicLabel": "Social movement typology",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "The Dravida Munnetra Khazagam (DMK) movement against the imposition of Hindi language is an example of",
      "options": [
        "Revolutionary Movement",
        "Resistance Movement",
        "Reforms Movement",
        "Utopian Movement"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 1,
      "explanation": "The DMK's anti-Hindi agitation opposed an imposed change (Hindi as sole official language) to protect the existing linguistic status quo, which is the defining trait of a resistance movement.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 It's like a neighbourhood pushing back when the city tries to force everyone to switch to one language sign overnight \u2014 resisting an imposed change, not trying to overthrow the whole system.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f 'Revolutionary Movement' sounds dramatic and fits the agitation's intensity, but revolutionary movements seek to overthrow the existing order, while DMK's protest was defensive, resisting a specific imposed change.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
      "year": 2016,
      "paperId": "mpsc-inspector-of-taxes-2016-gs-ii"
