      "subject": "economics",
      "topic": "gs2_economy",
      "topicLabel": "LPG reforms terminology",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "With reference to New Economic Policy in India, Liberalisation refers to",
      "options": [
        "transfer of ownership",
        "disinvestment",
        "deregulation",
        "licensing"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 2,
      "explanation": "Liberalisation means reducing government regulations and controls (like the License Raj) on private businesses, i.e. deregulation.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Liberalisation is like removing bureaucratic speed bumps from a road so businesses can drive faster without needing a permit at every turn.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f 'Disinvestment' is a real 1991-reforms term too (selling government stakes), but that's Privatisation, not Liberalisation, which specifically means cutting red tape.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
      "year": 2016,
      "paperId": "mpsc-inspector-of-taxes-2016-gs-ii"
