      "subject": "economics",
      "topic": "gs2_economy",
      "topicLabel": "National Income estimation body",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "Which of the following prepares the estimates of National Income in India?",
      "options": [
        "Central Statistical Organisation",
        "National Income Committee",
        "Planning commission",
        "Reserve Bank of India"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 0,
      "explanation": "The Central Statistical Organisation (CSO), now part of the National Statistical Office, is the official body responsible for compiling India's National Income estimates.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 CSO is like the official scorekeeper of the economy \u2014 tallying up everyone's earnings nationwide to report the final number.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Planning Commission (now NITI Aayog) is tempting since it deals with economic planning, but the actual number-crunching for National Income has always been the CSO's job.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
      "year": 2016,
