      "id": "mpsc-tax-0043",
      "subject": "economics",
      "topic": "gs2_economy",
      "topicLabel": "Basic economic terminology",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "GNP stands for",
      "options": [
        "General Net Product",
        "Gross National Product",
        "General Net Price",
        "Gross National Price"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 1,
      "explanation": "GNP stands for Gross National Product, the total value of goods and services produced by a country's residents, whether earned domestically or abroad.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 GNP is like counting your family's total earnings wherever they work in the world, not just what's earned inside your house (that's GDP).\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f 'General Net Product' sounds official but is a made-up term \u2014 the correct word is 'Gross', a common economics-terminology trap.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
