      "topic": "gs2_economy",
      "topicLabel": "Small-scale industry challenges",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "Which is the main problem of Small-scale industries?",
      "options": [
        "imbalanced regional development",
        "multi-purpose cooperative societies",
        "inferior quality of the products",
        "lack of financial resources"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 3,
      "explanation": "The most persistent and widely cited problem for India's small-scale industries is a lack of financial resources/access to credit, limiting their growth and modernisation.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Small-scale industries are like small shops trying to compete with a supermarket chain but with an empty cash register \u2014 the money problem holds everything else back.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f 'Inferior quality of products' is a tempting stereotype about small-scale goods, but the deeper, textbook-recognised root problem is financing, not quality.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
