      "subject": "economics",
      "topic": "gs2_economy",
      "topicLabel": "PMJDY features",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "Which of the following is not a feature of Pradhan Mantrijan DhanYojana?",
      "options": [
        "providing universal access to banking facilities",
        "providing basic bank accounts with overdraft facility and inbuilt accidental insurance",
        "financial literacy programme",
        "issuance of credit cards"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 3,
      "explanation": "PMJDY (launched 2014) gives basic zero-balance accounts with RuPay debit cards, overdraft, accident insurance, and financial literacy \u2014 but it never included issuing credit cards.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 PMJDY is like a starter banking kit \u2014 a basic account, a debit card, insurance, and a financial-literacy pamphlet \u2014 but no premium credit card in the box.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Debit/RuPay cards are genuinely part of the scheme, so 'credit cards' is an easy word-swap trap for people who mix up debit and credit.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
      "year": 2016,
      "paperId": "mpsc-inspector-of-taxes-2016-gs-ii"
