      "subject": "english",
      "topic": "eng_grammar",
      "topicLabel": "Parts of speech - adjectives",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "Identify the part of speech of the underlined word 'huge' in: 'I saw a huge caterpillar in the garden.'",
      "options": [
        "Adjective",
        "Adverb",
        "Verb",
        "Preposition"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 0,
      "explanation": "'Huge' describes the size of the noun 'caterpillar', which is the defining job of an adjective.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 'Huge' is a size-tag stuck on 'caterpillar' the same way 'tiny' or 'green' would be - all size/colour words are adjectives.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f None of the distractor options plausibly fit a size-word before a noun, so this one is straightforward.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
