      "answerIndex": 3,
      "explanation": "The adverb 'successfully' cleanly conveys that he succeeded in lifting the box, combining both ideas into one smooth sentence.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 'Successfully' is a single word doing the work of a whole extra sentence, like a one-word victory stamp added to the action.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f 'With success' is a wordy phrase substitute rather than the single adverb form the instruction actually calls for.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
