      "explanation": "'Overjoyed to hear' uses the infinitive to show the cause of the emotion - hearing the news caused the joy.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 'To hear' here works like a reason-tag stapled to a feeling word - 'overjoyed to hear' explains WHY he's overjoyed.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f 'Too overjoyed to hear' wrongly implies the joy PREVENTED him from hearing, the opposite of the intended meaning.",
