      "explanation": "'Not only' is placed right after the verb 'is', with 'but also' correctly linking the second quality, following the correct correlative word order.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 'Not only...but also' works like stacking two compliments on the same shelf - both need to sit right after 'is' in the correct order.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f 'Not only she is beautiful' misplaces 'not only' before the subject instead of after the verb, breaking standard correlative word order.",
