      "answerIndex": 2,
      "explanation": "'Invincible' means unable to be defeated or overcome - i.e. undefeatable - which is the closest matching option available.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Like a superhero whose skin can't be pierced - nothing can bring them down, they're undefeatable.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f 'Invisible' is a common sound-alike confusion with 'invincible', but they mean completely different things.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
