      "answerIndex": 0,
      "explanation": "The English East India Company was granted a royal charter by Queen Elizabeth I on 31 December 1600, giving it trading rights in Asia.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Think of it like a startup getting its business licence stamped on the last day of the year 1600 - that stamp is the whole reason 'East India Company' shows up in history from then on.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f 1601-1603 are just the following years and get thrown in as distractors since the charter date is easy to misremember by a year.",
