      "explanation": "The Regulating Act of 1773 designated the Governor of Bengal as the Governor-General of India, with authority over Bombay and Madras presidencies.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 It's like promoting the manager of your biggest branch office to CEO of the whole company - Bengal's governor got bumped up to boss of all British India.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Pitt's India Act (1784) is often confused with this because both deal with Company governance reforms, but the Governor-General title itself started with the 1773 Act.",
