      "explanation": "Wood's Despatch (1854) recommended a layered language policy - vernacular languages at the primary level and English at higher levels - not English-only instruction.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Think of it like a school policy that teaches you in your mother tongue in primary school and switches to English only once you reach college - never 'English only' from day one.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Because English education is so associated with British policy generally, it's tempting to assume Wood's Despatch pushed English exclusively.",
