      "explanation": "Warren Hastings is traditionally credited as the founder of the modern civil administration system in India that evolved into the Indian Civil Service.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Warren Hastings basically wrote the first employee handbook for running India as an administered territory - everyone after him (including Cornwallis) just revised his draft.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Cornwallis is a strong distractor because he formally organized the 'covenanted civil service' with fixed salaries and rules, so many textbooks credit him instead.",
