      "explanation": "Under Article 248, any subject not listed in the Union, State or Concurrent Lists automatically falls to Parliament (the Union Government) as a residuary power.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Think of the three lists as labelled kitchen drawers; whatever utensil doesn't fit any drawer just goes to the head chef (the Centre) by default.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f This is a common flip \u2014 many wrongly assume leftovers go to the States since states handle local matters, but India's federal design favours the Centre here.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
