      "explanation": "The Northern Plains are geologically young, formed by alluvial deposition mainly during and after the Pleistocene period, unlike the far older Peninsular plateau.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 The ancient Peninsular block is like an old stone foundation; the Northern Plains are the fresh silt 'carpet' laid down on top much more recently by rivers.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Siwaliks are actually the youngest (not oldest) range of the Himalayas, making option (c) a common reversal trap.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
      "year": 2019,
