      "answerIndex": 0,
      "explanation": "Bal Gangadhar Tilak coined this defiant slogan in 1916, asserting that self-rule (Swaraj) was an inherent right of Indians, not a favor to be granted.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 It's like declaring 'This is my house, and I'm walking in whether you like it or not' \u2014 Tilak was saying freedom wasn't a gift the British could withhold.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Bose is tempting because of his fiery reputation ('Give me blood...'), but that famous line is different and came decades later during WWII.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
      "year": 2021,
      "paperId": "mpsc-inspector-of-excise-&-narcotics-2021-gs-i"
