      "topicLabel": "Arya Samaj social reforms",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "Swami Dayanand 1. Attacked the spread of western sciences 2. Organized social services during natural calamities like flood 3. Encourage inter-caste marriage and widow remarriage 4. Opposed child marriages and polygamy Choose the correct answer from the following:",
      "options": [
        "2 and 3",
        "1, 2 and 3",
        "2, 3 and 4",
        "All of these"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 2,
      "explanation": "Dayanand Saraswati actively organized relief during famines/floods and pushed for inter-caste marriage, widow remarriage, and opposed child marriage and polygamy \u2014 but he did not reject Western science; the DAV schools he inspired taught modern science and English alongside Vedic studies.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Picture a strict grandfather who insists on old family values but still sends the kids to a modern school with science labs \u2014 Dayanand wasn't anti-science, just anti-superstition.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Statement 1 is tempting because Dayanand is often (wrongly) painted as anti-Western in a blanket sense, but his real target was superstition and idolatry, not science itself.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
