      "explanation": "Working through the clues places the five on the bench in the order E, B, A, C, D (left to right), which puts A directly between B and C.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Think of arranging five friends in a photo lineup using clues like \"so-and-so stands next to so-and-so\" until only one order fits - here, A ends up sandwiched between B and C.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f \"Between B and D\" looks plausible if you misplace D as adjacent to A instead of adjacent to C at the far right end.",
