      "answerIndex": 1,
      "explanation": "'Oh' is a sudden outburst of feeling tacked onto the sentence without grammatical connection to the rest; that is the definition of an interjection.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Interjections are like a gasp before you start talking; 'Oh!' is just noise expressing emotion, not part of the sentence's grammar.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
