      "subject": "english",
      "topic": "eng_vocab",
      "topicLabel": "Antonyms",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "'Dissent' is most opposite in meaning to:",
      "options": [
        "Object",
        "Concur",
        "Challenge",
        "Protest"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 1,
      "explanation": "'Dissent' means to disagree, so its opposite is 'Concur' (to agree).\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Dissent is voting 'no' in a meeting; concur is everyone else nodding 'yes' along with the decision.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f 'Object' and 'Protest' are near-synonyms of dissent itself, which can trick you into picking a word that means the same thing rather than the opposite.",
