      "subject": "english",
      "topic": "eng_vocab",
      "topicLabel": "Contextual word choice",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "Which word best fits the sentence: 'The judge's decision was widely considered ___ because it balanced law with compassion.'",
      "options": [
        "arbitrary",
        "biased",
        "lenient",
        "judicious"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 3,
      "explanation": "A decision that wisely balances law with compassion shows good, sound judgment; that is 'judicious'.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Judicious is like a chef balancing spice and sweetness perfectly in a dish, neither too harsh nor too soft.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f 'Lenient' is tempting since compassion is mentioned, but lenient implies going easy, while judicious captures the balanced wisdom of the whole decision.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
