      "question": "Water passes from soil to plant roots by a physical process called?",
      "options": [
        "Osmosis",
        "Diffusion",
        "Absorption",
        "Transpiration"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 0,
      "explanation": "Root hairs absorb water via osmosis, where water moves from the dilute soil solution into the more concentrated cell sap, across a semi-permeable membrane.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Water squeezes from a wet sponge into a drier sponge placed right next to it \u2014 the root cell is the thirstier sponge pulling water in.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f \"Absorption\" is tempting as a general everyday word for the same process, but the specific mechanism tested is osmosis.",
