      "answerIndex": 3,
      "explanation": "Two interleaved sequences run through the series: 2,4,6,8,10 (step +2) and 3,7,11,15,19 (step +4); the missing 10th term belongs to the second sequence, giving 19.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 It's like two people taking turns speaking \u2014 separate their sentences out and predict what the second person says next.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f \"13\" might tempt if you tried to continue the whole sequence with one single step pattern instead of splitting it into two interleaved series.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
