      "subject": "history",
      "topic": "gs1_history",
      "topicLabel": "Annexation of Awadh 1856",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "In 1856, the British finally annexed Awadh under the -",
      "options": [
        "Subsidiary Alliance",
        "Dual System",
        "Doctrine of Lapse",
        "Permanent Settlement"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 2,
      "explanation": "Awadh was annexed in 1856 by Lord Dalhousie; the exam intends 'Doctrine of Lapse' as the answer, though strictly the stated pretext was misgovernance rather than a lapsed heir.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Picture a landlord who normally only evicts tenants with no heir, but this time evicts a tenant anyway by claiming 'bad housekeeping' -- Awadh's annexation bent the Doctrine of Lapse logic to grab a well-run, wealthy state.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Subsidiary Alliance is tempting because Awadh had earlier accepted it, but the actual 1856 annexation trigger given in most keys is the Doctrine of Lapse option.",
