      "subject": "history",
      "topic": "gs1_history",
      "topicLabel": "Early revenue administration",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "In 1772, the revenue farming system was introduced by -",
      "options": [
        "Lord Wellesley",
        "Thomas Munro",
        "Lord Cornwallis",
        "Warren Hastings"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 3,
      "explanation": "Warren Hastings introduced the revenue farming (ijaradari) system in 1772, auctioning revenue collection rights to the highest bidder.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 It's like renting out your tax-collection job to whoever bids highest -- Hastings farmed out Bengal's revenue collection the same way in 1772.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Cornwallis is linked to land revenue too (Permanent Settlement, 1793) so people confuse the two systems and dates.",
