      "subject": "history",
      "topic": "gs1_history",
      "topicLabel": "Constitutional Acts - Governor-General",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "Which Act raised the status of Governor of Bengal to that of Governor-General?",
      "options": [
        "Pitt\u2019s India Act of 1784",
        "Regulating Act of 1773",
        "} Charter Act of 1793",
        "Charter Act of 1813"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 1,
      "explanation": "The Regulating Act of 1773 upgraded the Governor of Bengal to Governor-General of Bengal, with Warren Hastings becoming the first holder of that title.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 It's like a store manager being promoted to regional head office boss -- 1773's Act promoted the Bengal Governor into the first Governor-General.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Pitt's India Act (1784) and later Charter Acts refined the system further, tempting people who know later reforms but not the original 1773 upgrade.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
      "year": 2024,
      "paperId": "mpsc-group-b-combined-(state-tax-officer-/-cooperative-audit-officer)-2024-gs-i"
