      "explanation": "The Deccan Riots of 1875 saw peasants in Maharashtra attack Marwari and Gujarati moneylenders over exploitative debt and land seizure practices.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Think of villagers finally storming the loan-shark's office after years of being squeezed by debt -- that's the Deccan riots against Marwari-Gujarati moneylenders.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f 'British economic policy' is tempting as a general cause of rural distress, but the riot's direct target was the moneylenders, not British officials.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
      "year": 2024,
