      "explanation": "'Dastak' was a pass issued by East India Company officials allowing goods to move duty-free, a privilege that was widely misused and became a major grievance leading to conflicts like Buxar.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Think of it as a company employee's 'skip the toll booth' pass -- except the English started handing it out to private traders too, dodging taxes everywhere and angering local rulers.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f No option is strongly tempting here; the others are simply unrelated dictionary meanings.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
