      "answerIndex": 1,
      "explanation": "Mahadev Govind Ranade founded the Poona Sarvajanik Sabha in 1870, one of the earliest political associations in India.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Ranade basically opened the first 'citizens' forum' in Poona long before Congress existed -- a founding-father fact worth pinning on his name specifically.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Gokhale and Tilak are more famous Maharashtrian leaders, so people guess them instead of their mentor/senior Ranade.",
