      "subject": "history",
      "topic": "gs1_history",
      "topicLabel": "Print culture in colonial India",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "Printing Press in India was introduced by the -",
      "options": [
        "Dutch sailors",
        "Portuguese Jesuits",
        "Indian journalists",
        "English traders"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 1,
      "explanation": "The printing press was first brought to India by Portuguese Jesuit missionaries in Goa in 1556, mainly to print religious texts.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Missionaries brought the printing press the way you'd bring a photocopier to church -- to mass-produce religious pamphlets, and Goa in 1556 was the first stop.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f English traders are the tempting choice since English-language printing later dominated India, but they weren't first.",
