      "topicLabel": "Demand for Pakistan",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "Who was the Muslim leader to demand Pakistan in 1933?",
      "options": [
        "Muhamed Ali Jinah",
        "Rehmat Ali",
        "Maulana Azad",
        "JP Narayan"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 1,
      "explanation": "Chaudhry Rehmat Ali coined the term 'Pakistan' and first formally demanded a separate Muslim state in his 1933 pamphlet 'Now or Never'.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Rehmat Ali basically 'trademarked' the name Pakistan in a 1933 pamphlet, years before Jinnah picked up the political demand.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Jinnah is the face of Pakistan's creation later (1940 Lahore Resolution), so people wrongly credit him with the earliest 1933 demand too.",
