      "topic": "gs2_economy",
      "topicLabel": "LPG reforms 1991 - Narasimha Rao",
      "difficulty": "medium",
      "question": "The Policy of Liberalization, Privatization and Globalization was announced as New Economic Policy (NEP) by the Prime Minister -",
      "options": [
        "Indira Gandhi",
        "Narendra Modi",
        "Narasimha Rao",
        "Manmohan Singh"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 2,
      "explanation": "The 1991 New Economic Policy (Liberalisation, Privatisation, Globalisation) was launched under Prime Minister P.V. Narasimha Rao, with Manmohan Singh as his Finance Minister.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Narasimha Rao was the shopkeeper who decided to finally open the shutters to outside trade in 1991, with Manmohan Singh managing the till.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Manmohan Singh, as Finance Minister, is often mistakenly credited as PM for these reforms since he presented the actual budget speech.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
      "year": 2024,
