      "explanation": "Tools like ChatGPT are built on Artificial Neural Networks (specifically large transformer-based networks), which learn patterns in language from huge amounts of text.\n\n\ud83d\udca1 Think of a neural network as a huge web of tiny switches that learn, by trial and error over millions of examples, which switches to flip to produce a sensible reply \u2014 like training a huge choir to sing in tune by endless practice.\n\n\u26a0\ufe0f Blockchain and quantum computing are trendy tech buzzwords, which tempts people to associate them with any 'advanced AI', but they aren't what powers language models.",
      "source": "MPSC State Tax Officer / Group B Gazetted",
